[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Software Architecture Description for GentleBeam System (Gentlebeam SK Project)
UID: DHF-HRC-0004
METADATA:
  COMPONENT: heracles-software-architecture

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Purpose

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The purpose of this document is to describe the top-level architecture for the software components developed by Empyrean Medical Systems for the Voxel Ray GentleBeam system, known as Project Gentlebeam SK.

This document presents the software components from multiple points of view, describing the system context and logical software items, including SOUP (Software of Unknown Provenance) components, developer configurations, and other viewpoints.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Scope

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document describes the software components for the Voxel Ray GentleBeam system, known as Project Gentlebeam SK, at a high-level. The document does not address requirements, electro-mechanical designs, detailed software designs, or verification protocols (all of which other project documents cover).

The term Software relates to both software and firmware subsystems.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Terms and Definitions

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
**Architecture**: Organizational structure of a system or component.

**CM**: Configuration Management

**Configuration Item (CI)**: Entity that can be uniquely identified at a given reference point.

**Design History File (DHF)**: A compilation of specific records that describe the design history of a product.

**SW**: Software

**OTS**: Off-the-shelf

**Process**: Any activity that receives inputs and converts them into outputs.

**Product**: Components, manufacturing materials, in-process devices, finished devices, and returned devices.

**PRS**: Product Requirements Specification

**Regulatory Requirement**: A statutory requirement delineated within local, state, federal, or international regulations, applicable to the QMS, and employed for the manufacture of medical devices.

**Safety**: Freedom from unacceptable risk.

**Safety Defect**: An anomaly indicating a product malfunction that may affect the safe operation of the product and may pose harm to patients and/or users of the product.

**SBOM**: Software Bill of Materials

**Software Item**: Any identifiable part of a computer program, i.e., source code, object code, control code, control data, or a collection of these items.

**Software System**: Integrated collection of software items organized to accomplish a specific function or set of functions.

**Software Unit**: Software item that is not subdivided into other items (defined by the manufacturer).

**SOP**: Standard Operating Procedure

**Software of Unknown Provenance (SOUP)**: Software item that is already developed and generally available and that has not been developed for the purpose of being incorporated into the medical device (also known as "off-the-shelf software") or software item previously developed for which adequate records of the development processes are not available.

**Specification**: Any requirement with which a product, process, service, or other activity must conform.

**RTT**: Radiation Therapy Technician

**C&C**: Command and Control

**DAL**: Data Access Layer
<<<

